# Atelier Paper

An original MotionVault visual system. No company affiliation or claim of reproducing a named brand.

## Intent
Warm editorial restraint, paper surfaces, and generous literary typography. Designed for editorial experiences. Tone: Light. Density: Airy.

## Color palette
- Background: #eee9df (--paper). Primary canvas and page surfaces.
- Surface: #e3ded4 (--surface). Grouped content, inset panels, and quiet contrast.
- Text: #342e26 (--ink). Primary copy, navigation, and structural hierarchy.
- Secondary: #645f56 (--muted). Supporting descriptions and lower-emphasis labels.
- Accent: #b96540 (--accent). Selected states, focus, and deliberate expressive punctuation.
- Rule: #c9c4ba (--rule). Dividers and component boundaries; not small text.

Use text and background deliberately. Accent/background contrast: 3.47:1. This numeric relationship is not a claim that every accent/text combination is accessible; use ink for small functional copy and test actual foreground/background pairs.

## CSS tokens

```css
:root {
  --paper: #eee9df;
  --surface: #e3ded4;
  --ink: #342e26;
  --muted: #645f56;
  --accent: #b96540;
  --rule: #c9c4ba;
  --font-display: Georgia,serif;
  --font-body: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
  --font-meta: Courier New, monospace;
  --radius: 2px;
  --radius-control: 2px;
  --radius-card: 2px;
  --radius-media: 2px;
  --space-unit: 4px;
  --space-xs: 8px;
  --space-sm: 16px;
  --space-md: 24px;
  --space-lg: 48px;
  --space-xl: 96px;
  --shadow-card: none;
  --shadow-elevated: 0 24px 64px #342e2620;
  --layout-max: 1280px;
  --duration-control: 220ms;
  --duration-reveal: 550ms;
  --ease-out: cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1);
}
```

## Typography
Display: Georgia,serif; weight 400; 48–104px / 36–58px mobile; line-height 0.97–1.1; tracking -0.055em.
Body: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; 15–18px; line-height 1.6–1.85.
Metadata: Courier New, monospace; 10–12px; tracking 0.08em.
Keep prose below 65 characters per line. Functional labels remain readable; do not scale an entire desktop layout down to fit a phone. These system fonts need no remote font dependency.

## Space and layout
Base unit: 4px. Scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96px.
Use 24–32px within a thought and 64–96px between sections. Whitespace establishes hierarchy; do not fill every column.
Layout: Editorial split. 12 columns; 7 / 5 hero split. Max width: 1280px. Gutters: 6vw desktop / 7vw mobile.
Give the headline a broad quiet field and keep the visual counterweight on the right. Use short supporting copy and align section rules to the same page grid.
On phones, stack content in reading order, preserve practical touch targets, and allow useful horizontal overflow for dense data.

## Radii and shadows
Controls: 2px. Cards: 2px. Media: 2px.
Card shadow: none. Elevated shadow: 0 24px 64px #342e2620.
Use one coherent radius language. Reserve elevation for real layering.

## Components
- Navigation: Short meaningful labels, a stable wordmark, and one clear next action. Preserve visible keyboard focus.
- Buttons: Ink on paper for primary actions; 2px corners. Minimum 44px touch targets. Accent is available for focus and deliberate selected states.
- Cards & surfaces: Use surface contrast and thin rules for grouping. Keep elevation flat; avoid ornamental shadows.
- Forms & feedback: Persistent labels, readable 16px inputs, inline validation, useful error messages, and honest success states. Never use placeholder text as the only label.

## Interaction and motion
Control transitions: 220ms. Editorial reveals: 550ms. Easing: cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1).
Use restrained transform/opacity reveals to clarify sequence. Keep navigation and actions immediately available; motion should never delay access to content.
Honor prefers-reduced-motion, keep essential content visible, and never require hover to access an action. Provide clear focus, disabled, selected, error, loading, and success states.

## Applying this system with AI
Use the exact palette, typography roles, spatial rhythm, and component rules above to build the requested product. Create genuine information hierarchy and functional actions. Preserve warm editorial restraint, paper surfaces, and generous literary typography. The accompanying HTML is a composed visual-language example, not a claim about an existing business. Adapt its content and structure to the real task; do not add unrelated gradients, typefaces, badges, or fabricated customer claims.

